# opengrep / semgrep ignore — gate 4 (SAST).
#
# SAST targets EXECUTABLE SOURCE, not documentation prose or user-facing
# scaffolding templates. The "skills.*" auto rules match example/teaching code
# embedded in security-education docs (e.g. an intentional SQL-injection sample
# in skills/code-security/rules/sql-injection.md), which are false positives:
# the markdown is never executed. Secrets in ANY file are still covered by the
# separate gitleaks gate (5), so excluding docs here does not weaken secret
# detection.
#
# Keep this list narrow and greppable; do NOT add real source directories.

# Documentation / reference / instructional prose (example code is illustrative).
*.md

# User-facing scaffolding templates shipped for end users to copy (not this
# repo's own executable code); their CI/curl/workflow snippets are examples.
**/templates/

# Vendored third-party trees (also excluded at the CLI for other gates).
**/vendor/
# Same rationale, different suffix: tools/crcp/vendor_src/ holds vendored upstream
# codex-rs source. `**/vendor/` misses it by one suffix, which is why its upstream
# #[cfg(test)] PEM fixture reached the gate. Secrets here remain covered by gitleaks
# (gate 5) via a reasoned, path-scoped .gitleaks.toml waiver.
**/vendor_src/
**/node_modules/

# wfmon-export redaction test fixture: a synthetic transcript embedding FAKE
# example secrets (one per locked pattern) so the redactor can prove it masks
# them. Not executable source; secrets here are still covered by gitleaks (gate 5)
# via a reasoned .gitleaks.toml allowlist.
skills/workflow-monitor/fixtures/export/
# Same fixture, .agents/ mirror path introduced by the harness rescue (faae06d0).
.agents/skills/workflow-monitor/fixtures/export/

# use-vs-mention discriminator corpus: the recorded false-positive/positive-control
# fires for the harness's secret/command/marker guards, including one PEM-header and
# fake ghp_/AKIA bait so the discriminator can prove it distinguishes a real secret
# from a documented example. Not executable source (a .jsonl data fixture); secrets
# here are still covered by gitleaks (gate 5), which passes on it.
hooks/_shared/use-vs-mention-corpus.jsonl

# Vendored browser-profile trees (Chrome/Edge profile data + third-party extension
# bundles, e.g. Adobe Acrobat). Not this repo's executable source. Added 2026-10-31.
browser-profiles/
